The @indiannavy commissioned INS Nipun at the Naval Dockyard, Mumbai, in the presence of Chief of the Naval Staff Admiral Krishna Swaminathan. Speaking on the occasion, the Navy Chief described INS Nipun as a powerful addition to the Navy’s capabilities for multi-domain deep-water operations.

Lauding its over 75% indigenous content, Vice Admiral Sanjay Vatsayan, FOC-in-C, Western Naval Command, described the vessel as a testimony to India’s growing self-reliance in defence manufacturing.

The second Diving Support Vessel (DSV) of the Nistar-class, INS Nipun is equipped with advanced diving systems and underwater intervention capabilities, enabling sustained support to divers during demanding maritime operations.

